      "explanation": "Factor out the perfect-square parts so that both terms contain the same remaining square root. Using \\(\\sqrt{ab}=\\sqrt a\\sqrt b\\) for \\(a,b\\ge0\\), we get\n\\[\n\\sqrt8+\\sqrt{18}\n=\\sqrt{4\\cdot2}+\\sqrt{9\\cdot2}\n=2\\sqrt2+3\\sqrt2\n=5\\sqrt2.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{5\\sqrt2}\\), choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
      "id": "simplify-and-combine",
